# In a bot-versus-bot match outside analysis mode the human is a spectator, and
# the toolbar has always said so: Pass, Undo, Kibitz and all four navigation
# buttons are greyed. The commands behind them tested only isThinking(), which
# is a different question — the game loop clears playerToMove *before* its 500 ms
# inter-move sleep, so isThinking() is false for that window and every one of
# these keys was quietly accepted mid-match. Left and Home even called
# enterReview(), pausing a running match the buttons had refused to let anyone
# touch.
#
# match_mode_blocks_navigation.scn covers the same rule with two live engines,
# where it holds only because an engine usually happens to be thinking. This one
# is deterministic: the lock is set explicitly with `toggle ai vs ai` on a paused
# loaded game, so nothing is thinking at any point and the isThinking() term
# cannot mask a missing aiVsAiLocked term.

load_sgf tests/data/simple.sgf
wait_idle
expect main_line_moves 4
expect at_end true
expect phase paused

# Black human, White an engine: not both human, so analysis mode is available
# at the end. The loaded game stays paused, so neither ever gets to think.
switch_player black human
switch_player white mock
wait_idle
expect thinking false

# --- Baseline: unlocked, navigation works -----------------------------------
navigate_back
wait_idle
expect view_position 3
expect ai_vs_ai false

# --- Locked: every player action is refused ---------------------------------
toggle ai vs ai
wait_idle
expect ai_vs_ai true
expect mode match
expect thinking false          # the point: the lock is doing the work, not isThinking

navigate_back
wait_idle
expect view_position 3

navigate_start
wait_idle
expect view_position 3

navigate_forward
wait_idle
expect view_position 3

navigate_end
wait_idle
expect view_position 3

undo move
wait_idle
expect view_position 3

# Pass would create a pass variation here, since the cursor is mid-tree. Refused
# for the same reason, and the record must be untouched.
pass
wait_idle
expect view_position 3
expect main_line_moves 4
expect variations 1

play once
wait_idle
expect view_position 3
expect main_line_moves 4

# --- Analysis mode is the supported way in ----------------------------------
toggle_explore_mode
wait_idle
expect mode explore
# The toggle itself survives — only entering MATCH clears it. What lifts is the
# *lock*, which is the toggle and the mode together: aiVsAiLocked is
# (ai_vs_ai || both players are engines) && mode != analysis. Asserting the flag
# went false here would be asserting the wrong half of the rule.
expect ai_vs_ai true

navigate_start
wait_idle
expect view_position 0
expect black_stones 0
expect white_stones 0
